# VS Code REST Client: click Send Request above each call.
# Start: ./run.sh 2
# Automated verification: python3 verify.py --mode 2
# Complete expected bodies: expected/connexion2.json -> withoutNulls (default).
# To include nulls, stop the server and restart: ./run.sh 2 --include-nulls
# Then compare with withNulls and run verify.py --mode 2 --include-nulls.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8082/api

### Active versions and adapter: JSONProvider, includeNulls=false
# @name c2_runtime
GET {{baseUrl}}/demo/runtime
Accept: application/json

### Model: renamed properties, nested models, datetime/date/Decimal/UUID
# Expected: 200 application/json.
# createdAt="2024-04-05T06:07:08+00:00", birthday="2024-04-05", amount=12.5.
# note and child.comment are omitted by default.
# Complete body: expected/connexion2.json -> withoutNulls.model
# @name c2_model
GET {{baseUrl}}/demo/model
Accept: application/json

### List: [expected model]
# @name c2_list
GET {{baseUrl}}/demo/list
Accept: application/json

### Dictionary: {"primary": expected model}
# @name c2_map
GET {{baseUrl}}/demo/map
Accept: application/json

### Nulls: false, 0, and "" remain; optionalLabel and child.comment are omitted
# Complete body: expected/connexion2.json -> withoutNulls.nulls
# @name c2_nulls
GET {{baseUrl}}/demo/nulls
Accept: application/json

### OpenAPI document loaded by the generated application
# @name c2_openapi
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi.json
Accept: application/json

### Swagger UI: expected 200 text/html; open the URL in a browser to interact
GET {{baseUrl}}/ui/
